# Damage numbers (#321, sub-task 321.4): in the test playground every hit that damages an NPC shows the damage dealt
# as a number over the target - rising and fading for about a second, drawn in the world so both eyes see it at the
# target's depth. The game reports it as one `damage.number` event per number (entity, amount, and views = how many
# views drew it, with its screen position in each: x0 y0 x1 y1) and as status.json damageNumbers.visible (numbers on
# screen now). The original levels show nothing: damage-numbers-off.xrs.
#
# Runs in the generated playground (area 30) on the simulated headset:
#   .\scripts\dev\xrs-run.ps1 damage-numbers
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim idle -Sequence damage-numbers -Playground
# The playground's NPC (321.2) is reached through the channel, so the sequence needs no entity id: `playground place
# <ahead>` stands it ahead of the hero, facing him; `playground hit <n>` is the hero's hit of n damage on it (the
# damageCharacter() path every weapon, spell and missile ends in). The eye images are not compared: the NPC's hurt
# animation changes them as much as a number does - the event's views and positions say where each eye drew it.
@sim idle
@playground

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false

# The NPC held 80 units ahead of the hero
playground place 80
@frames 60
@assert damageNumbers.visible eq 0
@shot before-hit

# 1. One hit: one number, with the amount, on screen at once
@mark
playground hit 5
@until damageNumbers.visible ge 1 2s
@shot during-hit       # right away: a number lives 1.2 s game time (opaque 0.6 s) and a shot costs 0.3-0.7 s
# The event is logged 250 ms game time after the hit (hits on one target within 250 ms sum into one event)
@until events.byName."damage.number" ge 1 5s
@assert events.byName."damage.number" eq 1
# 2. In both eyes: the number was drawn in view 0 and view 1 (left and right eye on the headset)
@log damage\.number .*amount=5.*views=2

# 3. It fades: after about a second no number is on screen, and the event was not repeated
@until damageNumbers.visible eq 0 5s
@assert events.byName."damage.number" eq 1

# 4. A second hit: a second number
playground hit 5
@until events.byName."damage.number" ge 2 5s
@assert errors eq 0
